is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: dswa1, dswa2, dswb1, dswb2
diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the DHCP relay function on all distribution switches. The isc-dhcp-relay daemon is not running and has no configuration, so client DHCPDISCOVER broadcasts on the access VLAN SVIs are never forwarded to the DHCP server.

Mechanism: Existing clients keep working because they already have valid leases and default gateways, but newly booted hosts depend on the relay to reach the DHCP server in VLAN 30 (10.5.0.0/24). With the relay down/unconfigured, their broadcasts remain local and time out.

Localization: On dswa1, dswa2, dswb1, and dswb2:
- systemctl status shows isc-dhcp-relay “inactive (dead)” on all four.
- /etc/default/isc-dhcp-relay shows SERVERS="" and INTERFACES="" 
